// unit spotting chart
//
// Updated per change to camo / spotting algorithm for V1.52 patch
//
//   1. Choose base terrain that will provide 0 offset so that camo values in UNIT.DAT are the same:
//      Normal Planet / Grass Base Tile
//   2. Restrict max / min bonus beteween ±2 for most units, but allowing for a values outside this
//      range for "edge" cases
//   3. Due to restrictions, small offsets are used so that only edge cases for Foot units are +3:
//      this is restricted to Jungle planets with:
//      i. Mountain + Tree + Road + Structure on Grass, Desert, or Ice
//     ii. Hill + Tree + Road + Structure on Desert or Ice
//   4. For every structure, there is also a road tile, except for cities build on oceans so when
//      considering camo in structures, roads and structures are added together.
//      i. For structures on oceans, the ocean modifier for ground units is set to negate the structure's
//         bonus so that no additional camouflage is given (Wells & Shields - see STRBUILD.DAT)
//   5. For Naval and Underater units, delta subtracts 1 and river 2 from Naval (twice that for Underwater)
//
// V2015-02-21 (Matt): Added new Mech, Gate, and Underwater movement types
//
// names of terrains and tile set types MUST stay in the order below - note that desert is actually city
// for each type of terrain, lists the tile set type and the spotting modifiers
// for the movement types...foot, wheel, tread, air, naval, space, hover, jump,
// crawler, lander, mech, gate, and underwater.
//
// Note that all values are read in as floats and multiple terrain types are added
// together. There is also an additional modifier added to that camouflage value
// (see rand_camo_min & rand_camo_max in EFS.INI under the [Camo] heading) and then
// the final value is rounded up to the nearest integer (ceiling).
//
// Examples:
//  1. Artillery Wheel unit is on a normal planet with grass as base tile, then trees,
//     river, and then road. The Spotting is:
//     Grass =  0.00
//     Trees =  0.20
//     River = -1.05
//     Road =  -1.05
//     Artillery Camo = 2
//     Camouflage Rating = ( 0.0 + 0.2 + -1.05 + -1.05 ) + 2 = -1.9 + 2 = 0.1 (±2 random modifer)
//     so -1.9 to 2.1 for -1 to 3 (rounded up). Display is (red) for values below 2
//
//  2. Submarine Underwater unit on ocean jungle planet 
//     Ocean = 0.00
//     Submarine Camo = 8
//     Camouflage Rating = 8 + (±2 random modifer) so 6 to 10. Display is (green) from values above 8
//
//  3. Tracker Legion Foot unit is on jungle grass with trees and mountains
//     Grass = 0.00
//     Mountain = 0.30
//     Tree = 0.40
//     Tracker Legion Camo = 7
//     Camouflage Rating = ( 0 + 0.3 + 0.4 ) + 7 = 0.7 + 7 = 7.7 (±2 random modifer) 
//     so 5.7 to 9.7 for  6 to 10 (rounded up). Display is (green) for values > 7
//              
//  4. Hover Tank Hover unit on Desert (Actually City) Planet with Arid Grass with River
//     Arid Grass = -0.15
//     River = -1.0
//     Hover Tank Camo = 2
//     Camouflage Rating = ( -0.15 + -1.0 ) + 2 = -1.15 + 2 = 0.85 (±2 random modifer) 
//     so -1.15 to 2.85 for -1 to 3 (rounded up). Display is (red) for values below 2
//     
//  5. Space Carrier on Desert (Actually City) Planet with Desert tile
//     Desert = 0.0
//     Space Carrier Camo = 1
//     Camouflage Rating = 0.0 + 1 = 1 (±2 random modifer) 
//     so -1 to 3. Display is (red) for values below 1
//
//                    F     W     T     A     N     S     H     J     C     L     M     G     U
{ "ocean"                      
        "normal"   "-2.00 -1.00 -1.00  0.00  0.00 -0.95 -1.00 -0.95 -0.95 -0.95 -2.00 -0.95  0.00"
        "desert"   "-2.05 -1.05 -1.05  0.00  0.00 -1.00 -1.05 -1.00 -1.00 -1.00 -2.05 -1.00  0.00"
        "ice"      "-2.10 -1.10 -1.10  0.00  0.00 -1.05 -1.10 -1.05 -1.05 -1.05 -2.10 -1.05  0.00"
        "jungle"   "-2.15 -1.15 -1.15  0.00  0.00 -1.10 -1.15 -1.10 -1.10 -1.10 -2.15 -1.10  0.00"
        "barren"   "-1.95 -0.95 -0.95  0.00  0.00 -0.90 -0.95 -0.90 -0.90 -0.90 -1.95 -0.90  0.00"
}                     
